[{:db/id "q-107402/selection/faa0a805936d7477b6e8c3a4e1b72edc706e6801683939686b093d213dfcf2fe" :answer/id #uuid "80677a3e-179c-5307-8815-5716e23a8b1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107402/selection/bdd562effc9dc741363550760677c7fb4216f8161a9f536e0ab2e93923b21165" :answer/id #uuid "d02dc53c-5a99-59f8-b1c1-a33b49c094e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107402/selection/d6a9ee96cce3773ebdddd0b6e30e78558b6947c8fec77ad782391dd3ebdbb0bd" :answer/id #uuid "bc6cf462-d1ff-5367-8640-e982e089afea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107402/selection/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" :answer/id #uuid "c290a84a-2604-5ba5-b7ac-2cd67cd802da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107402/selection/1ac7ca9c0a955914010e7f058581f0190add50a0f726191f68df646470cb465e" :answer/id #uuid "75ea7e4b-dee0-5acb-8da9-102ec8dba84e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107402/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c33d0329-b852-5c2b-b2a2-03f0bcefea5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107402/selection/1ac7ca9c0a955914010e7f058581f0190add50a0f726191f68df646470cb465e" :answer-field/choices ["q-107402/selection/faa0a805936d7477b6e8c3a4e1b72edc706e6801683939686b093d213dfcf2fe" "q-107402/selection/bdd562effc9dc741363550760677c7fb4216f8161a9f536e0ab2e93923b21165" "q-107402/selection/d6a9ee96cce3773ebdddd0b6e30e78558b6947c8fec77ad782391dd3ebdbb0bd" "q-107402/selection/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" "q-107402/selection/1ac7ca9c0a955914010e7f058581f0190add50a0f726191f68df646470cb465e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107402" :question/id #uuid "d74f8b68-3c0c-59b0-82f5-fe441f002de9" :question/math-academy-id "q-107402" :question/problem "Express $z=-2\\text{i}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ We get\n\n$$\nz=0+(-2)\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=0+(-2)\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n      \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=0$  and $y=-2$ is negative, $z$ lies on the negative $y$-axis. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z=-2\\text{i}$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107402/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a6128-22df-5a02-96fd-7c8cabf8f5f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107402"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-322671/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6994327e-554f-5047-8669-377864db641e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322671/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c67356ce-7c2c-5ea0-b7d7-c30c1897900f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322671/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a99b96f3-30f8-5e7a-b729-8240c479729a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322671/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-322671/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-322671/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322671/field-2/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" :answer/id #uuid "e518ec0d-10d6-5d05-84eb-da99797d902b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322671/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "801da17f-b817-5874-96d7-3440b4026507" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322671/field-2/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-322671/field-2/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322671/field-3/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" :answer/id #uuid "8001af7b-8610-54cc-9c1c-676bcb3e1f74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322671/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc54cab-ae38-552f-a1af-c3c8cf6538e6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322671/field-3/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-322671/field-3/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322671" :question/id #uuid "315a769c-4170-5163-b093-33a48aeaf82a" :question/math-academy-id "q-322671" :question/problem "Express $z=\\sqrt{3}-\\text{i}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give the **exact** values of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ in **radians** from $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(${{field-2}}$)+\\,i\\operatorname{sin}⁡(${{field-3}}$))$" :question/worked-solution "In polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\sqrt{3}-\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $ represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\sqrt{3}>0$ and $y=-1<0,$ $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{3}}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z=\\sqrt{3}-\\text{i}$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{6}))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-322671/field-1" "q-322671/field-2" "q-322671/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a6128-22df-5a02-96fd-7c8cabf8f5f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-322671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107404/selection/cec3927ed937a9d8279acce734fd6c8b6542e1d2516f1f70a33c267906e827cd" :answer/id #uuid "47635084-efa7-5caa-8f5a-79257e4932d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107404/selection/f0a9d2d469f40d4152561f1fc088b896d004b3c2e908a8fa1d7c2d5cf11b1d6f" :answer/id #uuid "eda9688d-579f-5fa8-85b7-ca355922a5c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107404/selection/3074a744b107eb1a93eec95fa394b5247bcbb6033e5632172bbdbd070bdd0901" :answer/id #uuid "c3176ea4-f443-50f2-8b30-b3818482e106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107404/selection/1abfaba4db7f38a887154975dd9ec9351108f16f531b1393503f216fccbb9a17" :answer/id #uuid "4e63922c-9952-5728-840a-ddb17d6091b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107404/selection/0a6bbafdb9b5079d29608553d117a5c4eb5abb68eb77fc89ebe39507cdf4cd42" :answer/id #uuid "37fe3d7e-4b95-5d99-b141-cd7c35573b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107404/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5b8cd4e-2ca5-5f25-83bd-999a34e1c748" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107404/selection/0a6bbafdb9b5079d29608553d117a5c4eb5abb68eb77fc89ebe39507cdf4cd42" :answer-field/choices ["q-107404/selection/cec3927ed937a9d8279acce734fd6c8b6542e1d2516f1f70a33c267906e827cd" "q-107404/selection/f0a9d2d469f40d4152561f1fc088b896d004b3c2e908a8fa1d7c2d5cf11b1d6f" "q-107404/selection/3074a744b107eb1a93eec95fa394b5247bcbb6033e5632172bbdbd070bdd0901" "q-107404/selection/1abfaba4db7f38a887154975dd9ec9351108f16f531b1393503f216fccbb9a17" "q-107404/selection/0a6bbafdb9b5079d29608553d117a5c4eb5abb68eb77fc89ebe39507cdf4cd42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107404" :question/id #uuid "6a55cea2-0632-5c86-ad59-90081e2751a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-107404" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{1-\\text{i}}{4}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ We get\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{1-\\text{i}}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}+(-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{1}{4}+(-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\frac{1}{4}$ is positive and $y=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is negative, $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{4})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z=\\frac{1-\\text{i}}{4}$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107404/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a6128-22df-5a02-96fd-7c8cabf8f5f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107404"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8263/selection/b9ecf89b4582ab433e4398dc8f884e5cab9f91f7072ab7333c3fef6f031a5a23" :answer/id #uuid "45dd2f36-ec7d-5a79-b200-797ca20b4ab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{15}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.486)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.486))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8263/selection/b4c3e9177a7e9f9d270e184eaa99efce3439fb7e572a51282d578b4af8f9ba49" :answer/id #uuid "eed5f1af-d029-5e1e-94f1-ca93d6cc81ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=13(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.641)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.641))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8263/selection/da504db3eba4b4ee41d13ad3a3af3f72be655812b9eb4f8be2eb3e8de0858ba5" :answer/id #uuid "1307e854-092c-561e-b48c-d3ed760d21fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.176)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.176))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8263/selection/eb3708150a99529b9460e99608be7488785de9d05d0d8ff58ca275c57b437fc9" :answer/id #uuid "acbe0745-cd41-5df6-af32-46a37b60791d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=15(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.723)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.723))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8263/selection/06bedc09d428f197390560ae1181b3cf876387d751858ea80e9732e69c07b2a2" :answer/id #uuid "81f5da0c-510f-5e35-b0ee-287b70870625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=13(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.176)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.176))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8263/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef841a54-aec6-536f-8438-e9e88ec75019" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8263/selection/06bedc09d428f197390560ae1181b3cf876387d751858ea80e9732e69c07b2a2" :answer-field/choices ["q-8263/selection/b9ecf89b4582ab433e4398dc8f884e5cab9f91f7072ab7333c3fef6f031a5a23" "q-8263/selection/b4c3e9177a7e9f9d270e184eaa99efce3439fb7e572a51282d578b4af8f9ba49" "q-8263/selection/da504db3eba4b4ee41d13ad3a3af3f72be655812b9eb4f8be2eb3e8de0858ba5" "q-8263/selection/eb3708150a99529b9460e99608be7488785de9d05d0d8ff58ca275c57b437fc9" "q-8263/selection/06bedc09d428f197390560ae1181b3cf876387d751858ea80e9732e69c07b2a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8263" :question/id #uuid "7039d956-de07-5ae4-acb5-d43443cbc317" :question/math-academy-id "q-8263" :question/problem "Express $z=5+12\\text{i}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give $\\theta $ in radians to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=5+12\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=5$ is positive and $y=12$ is positive, $z$ lies in the first quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{12}{5}) \\\\  & ≈1.176,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. \n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z=5+12\\text{i}$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=13(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.176)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1.176))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8263/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a6128-22df-5a02-96fd-7c8cabf8f5f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-322670/field-1/e777f41c0e8bccdd1c54f16ea0ca8d5a45a8d4390fe17bd33384b645d44fa8c3" :answer/id #uuid "b9102fc8-66b5-5764-959c-6d358d657262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{146}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322670/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9b5150-a9f6-58f0-bbd2-eba50485fcfb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322670/field-1/e777f41c0e8bccdd1c54f16ea0ca8d5a45a8d4390fe17bd33384b645d44fa8c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-322670/field-1/e777f41c0e8bccdd1c54f16ea0ca8d5a45a8d4390fe17bd33384b645d44fa8c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322670/field-2/ca42f713739e2903834e78df28595c239f293cab757efc946414bbd2c7618909" :answer/id #uuid "4651e956-a7d3-5a0c-91ef-9421c4100c29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322670/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfeb19ad-6ad8-5879-94e2-87865549622b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322670/field-2/ca42f713739e2903834e78df28595c239f293cab757efc946414bbd2c7618909" :answer-field/choices ["q-322670/field-2/ca42f713739e2903834e78df28595c239f293cab757efc946414bbd2c7618909"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322670/field-3/ca42f713739e2903834e78df28595c239f293cab757efc946414bbd2c7618909" :answer/id #uuid "b8c74103-c25c-584b-90a8-f8bbe35b8afd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322670/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "f46f5889-a17e-5a81-b630-a85f8a045c6d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322670/field-3/ca42f713739e2903834e78df28595c239f293cab757efc946414bbd2c7618909" :answer-field/choices ["q-322670/field-3/ca42f713739e2903834e78df28595c239f293cab757efc946414bbd2c7618909"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322670" :question/id #uuid "ff3a2f18-7dab-5d55-9d4f-1b11e3d4584c" :question/math-academy-id "q-322670" :question/problem "Express $z=5-11\\text{i}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give the **exact** value of $r$ and round $\\theta $ in **radians** from $[0,2\\pi )$ to **two decimal places**.\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(${{field-2}}$)+i\\operatorname{sin}⁡(${{field-3}}$))$" :question/worked-solution "In polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=5-11\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-11)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+121} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{146}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=5$ is positive and $y=-11$ is negative, $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-11}{5}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -arctan\\,(\\frac{11}{5}) \\\\  & ≈5.14,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places. \n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z=5-11\\text{i}$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{146}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5.14)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5.14))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-322670/field-1" "q-322670/field-2" "q-322670/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a6128-22df-5a02-96fd-7c8cabf8f5f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-322670"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321383/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6f6b0b43-3aa0-5a9f-8e41-d32abc3440f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321383/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "002e8fa8-e9da-5939-86d8-da7a025abab4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321383/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-321383/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321383/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3" :answer/id #uuid "f085ef27-3b20-5223-84d6-b64ed58a461f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321383/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "22bbd87f-fdc4-59ff-8f2d-69ce3ba0e451" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321383/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3" :answer-field/choices ["q-321383/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321383/field-3/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3" :answer/id #uuid "cf9cc000-d0fc-5e90-832c-63299bc9d485" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321383/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "7385871f-7cdf-55f8-8b65-df5356f87329" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321383/field-3/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3" :answer-field/choices ["q-321383/field-3/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321383" :question/id #uuid "a15e3b43-5e5e-572b-a4ef-754d820846a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-321383" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{4}{1+\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give the **exact** values of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ in **radians** from $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(${{field-2}}$)+i\\operatorname{sin}⁡(${{field-3}}$))$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{4}{1+\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3})}{(1+\\text{i}\\sqrt{3})(1-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-4\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}}{{1}^{2}-{(\\text{i}\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-4\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}}{1-(-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-4i\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{3}\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=1-\\sqrt{3}\\,i,$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=1$ and $y=-\\sqrt{3},$ $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=2\\cdot \\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321383/field-1" "q-321383/field-2" "q-321383/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321383"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86605/selection/3074a744b107eb1a93eec95fa394b5247bcbb6033e5632172bbdbd070bdd0901" :answer/id #uuid "4931231f-8fe2-5d63-930a-9fad33a60565" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86605/selection/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" :answer/id #uuid "5be99101-da47-5b60-a7ff-1d4866ac49dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86605/selection/3952566346facdc42db30c544c6d44833224281a6426ca0af17124794e116355" :answer/id #uuid "d395ff26-bd69-5d3e-a7a3-80b698bce481" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86605/selection/faa0a805936d7477b6e8c3a4e1b72edc706e6801683939686b093d213dfcf2fe" :answer/id #uuid "f6eebcb8-c6f5-5f89-b376-0b5ac080a01f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86605/selection/ac5d8ae84a264765e5c6609e86f2241ac0b2c55f73649d0aad8d29a28be07b09" :answer/id #uuid "e383b42a-a1f0-518f-85ba-2169a6672380" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86605/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6bbc968-c9c1-56e3-a177-4ae86e3b8b16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86605/selection/3074a744b107eb1a93eec95fa394b5247bcbb6033e5632172bbdbd070bdd0901" :answer-field/choices ["q-86605/selection/3074a744b107eb1a93eec95fa394b5247bcbb6033e5632172bbdbd070bdd0901" "q-86605/selection/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" "q-86605/selection/3952566346facdc42db30c544c6d44833224281a6426ca0af17124794e116355" "q-86605/selection/faa0a805936d7477b6e8c3a4e1b72edc706e6801683939686b093d213dfcf2fe" "q-86605/selection/ac5d8ae84a264765e5c6609e86f2241ac0b2c55f73649d0aad8d29a28be07b09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86605" :question/id #uuid "1a69f1b0-3405-5ab6-ad35-05b2ddc39c21" :question/math-academy-id "q-86605" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{2}{1+\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1-\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{2}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\text{i})}{(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\text{i})}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\text{i})}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\text{i})}{2} \\\\  & =1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=1-\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=1$ is positive and $y=-1$ is negative, $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-1}{1}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86605/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86605"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107504/selection/6f4d684d2e2e09c876fcb295e00fc38663b28c2303088f741e6e1c58cc1ab5f2" :answer/id #uuid "df65c59e-9e0d-50e5-a29f-22ee643f6a97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107504/selection/7438c1510e77bb16170a7fc6c425f6c1ce9b26a7b4a28c9b636236b4aedcb152" :answer/id #uuid "a79c9618-9d26-5d61-bd73-ff3ad0033cdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107504/selection/1564b74c4c0795842f54bd3f16eff3c5d44b977784d637ed0710df9981ef629b" :answer/id #uuid "79662cb1-82d2-5532-aa08-286b903c8ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107504/selection/adf741c8d4fd79987785071080763e979fe975b6e37486007160cabcd031d201" :answer/id #uuid "f35b0eec-3c71-5b02-a35e-42d4423a20fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{4}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107504/selection/3698092054463ef18760f2ab98a31f683fad9b3714eb5d3516ea3820d7f28923" :answer/id #uuid "c42f919a-0c91-5215-8bfb-970af4dd5aa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{4}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107504/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e588cbb-f092-53bf-8fa5-011809180929" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107504/selection/1564b74c4c0795842f54bd3f16eff3c5d44b977784d637ed0710df9981ef629b" :answer-field/choices ["q-107504/selection/6f4d684d2e2e09c876fcb295e00fc38663b28c2303088f741e6e1c58cc1ab5f2" "q-107504/selection/7438c1510e77bb16170a7fc6c425f6c1ce9b26a7b4a28c9b636236b4aedcb152" "q-107504/selection/1564b74c4c0795842f54bd3f16eff3c5d44b977784d637ed0710df9981ef629b" "q-107504/selection/adf741c8d4fd79987785071080763e979fe975b6e37486007160cabcd031d201" "q-107504/selection/3698092054463ef18760f2ab98a31f683fad9b3714eb5d3516ea3820d7f28923"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107504" :question/id #uuid "c0791cfa-321a-5888-9413-89be1eb2fcca" :question/math-academy-id "q-107504" :question/problem "Express $z=-\\frac{2}{3\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $-3\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{2}{3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(-3\\text{i})}{(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\text{i}}{-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\text{i}}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}=0+\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i},$ the magnitude is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=0$  and $y=\\frac{2}{3}$ is positive, $z$ lies on the positive direction of the $y$-axis. So,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107504/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107504"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86606/selection/af003d1077f3d7090c6ec4a35e489fcc4488bec526042d86bde7b9d8bc528aac" :answer/id #uuid "0dc38f84-814f-5d77-ac08-3cc5d500805e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4.234)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4.234)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86606/selection/25642a2ad92c576086f390f0f7b2365853f8e872ef427fddd9374b9df906d13d" :answer/id #uuid "f850bdda-0b2b-549b-bb53-bc93ccbb9d89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5.640)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5.640)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86606/selection/7bb2976fd0e49e1c5a81f2b46d10c4920a8a8a45e1e6462f74783aa2db3a5497" :answer/id #uuid "091da9c1-57f8-539d-a586-9bd526967168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4.234)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4.234))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86606/selection/a9fc7ff6b64477adfeabc87acd77c0dc9852e3aba54c8d575bb854368eec7745" :answer/id #uuid "c9db56d6-479f-50c5-aa63-c586f774158a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5.640)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5.640))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86606/selection/7202062e10d2d5cb0154276e68c1462894d4b1bbce3d104b80d11ac8aaa10e19" :answer/id #uuid "3809dc0c-e1da-5a4a-a5c1-7603dd3a2e94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3.348)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3.348)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86606/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd2208e-a3d0-5013-ab08-0adf2908cb77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86606/selection/25642a2ad92c576086f390f0f7b2365853f8e872ef427fddd9374b9df906d13d" :answer-field/choices ["q-86606/selection/af003d1077f3d7090c6ec4a35e489fcc4488bec526042d86bde7b9d8bc528aac" "q-86606/selection/25642a2ad92c576086f390f0f7b2365853f8e872ef427fddd9374b9df906d13d" "q-86606/selection/7bb2976fd0e49e1c5a81f2b46d10c4920a8a8a45e1e6462f74783aa2db3a5497" "q-86606/selection/a9fc7ff6b64477adfeabc87acd77c0dc9852e3aba54c8d575bb854368eec7745" "q-86606/selection/7202062e10d2d5cb0154276e68c1462894d4b1bbce3d104b80d11ac8aaa10e19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86606" :question/id #uuid "9b4fd445-6363-58ec-83c1-a1c688bd3d69" :question/math-academy-id "q-86606" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{5}{4+3\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give $\\theta $ in radians to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $4-3\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{5}{4+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(4-3\\text{i})}{(4+3\\text{i})(4-3\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(4-3\\text{i})}{{4}^{2}-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(4-3\\text{i})}{16+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(4-3\\text{i})}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}+\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16+9}{25}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{25}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $ represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\frac{4}{5}$ is positive and $y=-\\frac{3}{5}$ is negative, $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{5})}{(\\frac{4}{5})}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & ≈5.640,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. \n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5.640)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5.640)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86606/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86606"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321420/field-1/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980" :answer/id #uuid "cc85c43c-6e60-58d9-92cf-ac6b866cbd04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321420/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "23abaa5c-f7c3-522a-b38a-bd916814fcda" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321420/field-1/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980" :answer-field/choices ["q-321420/field-1/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321420/field-2/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203" :answer/id #uuid "ce211202-f488-5b66-b236-b347c5372f07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321420/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ede24cf6-2533-555c-9c03-dd872dc4268b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321420/field-2/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203" :answer-field/choices ["q-321420/field-2/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321420/field-3/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203" :answer/id #uuid "ebca2134-f62d-594a-abe2-3a5853b396c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321420/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7b65906-25ce-5d9d-b427-3a70d48b6883" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321420/field-3/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203" :answer-field/choices ["q-321420/field-3/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321420" :question/id #uuid "752642e1-ccd9-52f8-95c0-e1145873311a" :question/math-academy-id "q-321420" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{3}{1-\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give the **exact** values of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ in **radians** from $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(${{field-2}}$)+i\\operatorname{sin}⁡(${{field-3}}$))$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1+\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{3}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1+\\text{i})}{(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1+\\text{i})}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1+\\text{i})}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1+\\text{i})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{9}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $y=\\frac{3}{2}$ are both positive, $z$ lies in the first quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{3}{2}}{\\frac{3}{2}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321420/field-1" "q-321420/field-2" "q-321420/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321420"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321308/field-1/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "de5b5483-73b3-5573-ac1e-7366ffa3d670" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321308/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "428114ef-f99b-5a0c-bd59-0a50139b6ed2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321308/field-1/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer-field/choices ["q-321308/field-1/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321308/field-2/a1718737dbd495fb450a9cad74f457749b10e8bf5f8306a2293022758aa6513c" :answer/id #uuid "084e2a44-0684-54ed-a68d-1ba9e0d5c955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321308/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "812b51ab-1051-52ae-8a2b-4f6b21a262fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321308/field-2/a1718737dbd495fb450a9cad74f457749b10e8bf5f8306a2293022758aa6513c" :answer-field/choices ["q-321308/field-2/a1718737dbd495fb450a9cad74f457749b10e8bf5f8306a2293022758aa6513c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321308" :question/id #uuid "14c208bb-1cd0-520c-8ca7-4565597bcd35" :question/math-academy-id "q-321308" :question/problem "Express $z=18(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}))$ in the form $z=x+y\\,\\text{i},$ where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers. Give the **exact** values of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+$\n{{field-2}}\n$i$" :question/worked-solution "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nFirst, we find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the values and expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =18(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =18(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\text{i}\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{2}+\\text{i}\\,\\frac{18\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =-9+9\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321308/field-1" "q-321308/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31e4455a-9f8f-5c12-8c96-bb6735691591"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321306/field-1/8ec505df16daf210999fdc78388da8154af0ca3a9fdfb88f6701faa823cd03b2" :answer/id #uuid "aa47ac83-c599-5d64-af74-0ce01009fe9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321306/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "81d5b7b8-1e23-5286-8b92-58f13aa4a4bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321306/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d289dd6-ff07-598b-b6e7-32365c0d6cd7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321306/field-1/8ec505df16daf210999fdc78388da8154af0ca3a9fdfb88f6701faa823cd03b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-321306/field-1/8ec505df16daf210999fdc78388da8154af0ca3a9fdfb88f6701faa823cd03b2" "q-321306/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321306/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "5abc8bf4-c3af-5169-a683-057544f14d2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321306/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3b92e6